  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Iran: Trade-Related Technical Assistance</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project &#x201c;EU &#x2013; Iran Trade Development: Trade-related technical assistance, capacity building, and value chain development for inclusive and sustainable trade-led growth in Iran&#x201d; is part of the renewed cooperation and engagement between the EU and Iran following the conclusion of the JCPOA. Over the course of five years, the project aims at increasing and diversifying trade in goods and services. It focuses on the development of a National Export Strategy as well as sectoral export strategies, further developing selected value chains. Private sector support is at the core of the project to allow for Iranian MSMEs to increase their competitiveness and gain international market access. Furthermore, the project provides technical assistance to Iran&apos;s Trade Promotion Organization (ITPO), enabling the organization to offer better services to their members. With a strong focus on youth, the project set up a youth entrepreneurship and youth trade accelerator programme. The activities and efforts under the project are closely connected to Iran&#x2019;s National Development Plan 2016-2021, and in line with the European Consensus on Development and the UN 2030 Agenda for Sustainable Development.</narrative>
  </description>
